  "id": "zero-sum-game",
  "term": "zero-sum game",
  "definition": "In social psychology, a zero-sum game refers to viewing social relationships as inherently antagonistic, so that one person’s or group’s gain is seen as coming at another’s expense when resources are limited. It describes a belief that benefits and losses are linked in a fixed trade-off.",
